messages:
maria: FYI AcmeCorp (customer) opened a ticket - their SSO tokens started getting 403s for embeddings + rerank after an IDP change. They see missing-scope errors in prod :confused:

support-bot: Ticket #AC-12487 created, priority P1 (customer blocking).

alex: Can you paste the exact curl they used and the 403 body?

maria: Sure — repro from their env (redacted):

curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/embeddings 
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <SSO_TOKEN>" 
  -d '{"input":"hello"}'

HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden
{
  "error": "insufficient_scope",
  "message": "missing scope: rerank"
}

maria: We asked them to introspect token; this is the JWT payload they pasted (claims trimmed):
{
  "sub": "user:acme/1234",
  "iss": "https://idp.acme.com/",
  "scope_versions": ["v2:infer", "v2:rerank", "v2:embeds"],
  "exp": 1765558000
}

kyle: Huh - they replaced the old flat "scopes" string with a namespaced "scope_versions" array and prefixed values (v2:...). Our auth middleware only checks for the `scopes` or `scope` claim and looks for exact tokens like "embeddings", "rerank", "inference". So it never matched their v2: values.

alex: Reproduced locally by swapping my token to include scope_versions. Same 403.

kyle: Quick mitigation: accept a fallback claim and normalize prefixes. Patch idea (pseudo):

```
// auth/claims.go
scopes := []string{}
if claims["scopes"] != nil {
  scopes = parseScopes(claims["scopes"].(string))
} else if claims["scope_versions"] != nil {
  raw := claims["scope_versions"].([]string)
  for _, s := range raw {
    // strip vN: prefix if present
    if idx := strings.Index(s, ":"); idx != -1 {
      s = s[idx+1:]
    }
    // map short aliases
    if s == "embeds" { s = "embeddings" }
    scopes = append(scopes, s)
  }
}
// then continue checks against normalized scopes
```

kyle: Minimal and low-risk; adds normalization + alias map. I can put up a canary to staging.

jess: +1. Please include unit tests for array handling and alias mapping. Also add a log line so we can see when we hit the fallback path: `auth: used scope_versions fallback` :eyes:  

maria: Customer workaround while we patch: use a Console-created API key (non-SSO) or have their IdP admin change the scope names to the legacy flat claim temporarily. Both are fine short-term. I sent the workaround steps to the customer.

alex: I ran the patch locally and added tests. Repro before fix: 403. After applying normalization: 200 OK for embeddings + rerank endpoints.

kyle: I'll push a small PR with tests and request an expedited review. Plan: canary to staging (30m), smoke run, then prod rollout if clean.

ops-bot: Deploy pipeline started for branch fix/scope-normalize -> staging.

jess: tagging infra for observability: add histogram for `auth.fallback_scope_versions` and a debug metric increment when the fallback is used. We'll monitor for any surge.

maria: Noted. I've updated the support ticket with repro steps + temporary workaround and ETA for fix (couple hours). Customer replied they can use console API key for now and asked for a postmortem once resolved.

kyle: After prod rollout we'll also add a migration doc for IDP integrators: note that if you prefix scopes (v2:...), we accept them but recommend mapping to canonical names.

maria: Thanks team — keeping this thread. Will update ticket when prod fix is live :thumbsup:

support-bot: Ticket #AC-12487 updated: status -> awaiting prod verification.
